course: dictionary
lesson: 3394
title: Expel: send out or push out
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expel is a verb, and its forms change: expels, expelled, expelling. When a pupil is expelled, they are made to leave their school for good, because they behaved very badly. It is the most serious punishment a school can give.
explain: Expel can also mean forcing someone to leave a country, a club or a group. Imagine a story where a hero is expelled from a kingdom. The word tells you the hero did not leave by choice. Someone made them go.
explain: Expel has a science meaning too. To expel something is to push it out with force. Your lungs expel air when you breathe out, and your heart expels blood around your body. Here, nobody is in trouble, and the word simply describes a push.
explain: Use the swap test to check your meaning. Put "push out" or "send away" into the sentence in place of expel. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: «Expel» means to make someone leave a school, country, club or group, or to push something out with force.
fact: To be expelled from school means to be made to leave for good, because of very bad behaviour.
fact: In the US, the same punishment is called "expulsion".
fact: In science, lungs expel air and the heart expels blood.
fact: Expel is a verb, so its forms are expels, expelled and expelling.
exercise: «The pupil was expelled from school for very bad behaviour.» What does expelled mean here? | Moved to the front of the class | *Made to leave school for good | Given a prize for good work | Allowed to stay late
exercise: In science, «Your lungs expel air when you breathe out.» What does expel mean? | Keep safe inside | *Push out with force | Pull in gently | Make warm
exercise: «The hero was expelled from the kingdom.» What does this tell you? | The hero built a new castle | The hero was crowned as king | *The hero was forced to leave the kingdom | The hero asked to dance
test: «Your heart expels blood around your body.» What does expels mean? | Warms it up | *Pumps it out with force | Stops it completely | Keeps it for later
test: In the US, what is another word for being expelled from school? | *Expulsion | Exit | Excursion | Exposure
exam: Which sentence uses expel to mean forcing someone out of a group? | The heart expelled blood. | The lungs expelled the air. | The class expelled a loud cheer. | *The council expelled the member from the club for cheating.
